OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`. That path
does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real, compiled canonical
page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by the DONE sibling automations pages
(AutomationCardPage, AutomationActivityFeedPage, AutomationsListPage, all under
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/`). `Sources` is a project.yml source path
(createIntermediateGroups), shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002); both consume the KMP
shared core as `Shared.xcframework` (ADR-004). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only deviation
from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9.

REUSE (DRY): a fully-stated feature-view already ships at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/
ConflictWarnings.{swift,Model,Views,Adapter,Previews,strings}` (artifact 0084 — the canonical parity
of the web component, with the loading / empty / error / conflicts branches, the P4 stale+offline
chips, severity→SF-Symbol mapping, the `"{name}": {reason}` body, VoiceOver, and the P2 tokens). Like
the sibling AutomationCardPage hosts the shared `AutomationCard` view, this page HOSTS that feature-view
rather than re-implementing it, and drives it with a thin `@Observable` page model. No feature-view file
was edited (it belongs to a different artifact's allowed-files — covenant #7).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `ConflictWarnings` is a presentational leaf the automation builder (under the `/automations`
route owned by `AutomationsList`) renders inline — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a
top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack AutomationsList's route). Instead it ships a typed
`NavigationDestination` seam — `ConflictWarningsLink` + `View.conflictWarningsDestination()` +
`ConflictWarningsRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link the
screen, mirroring the DONE siblings. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) or any
sibling surface were made (covenant #7).

